{"content_hash": "dfe6785705969f25", "version_id": 638, "article_id": 64, "level_code": "ja_n3", "lang": "ja", "level": 3, "level_label": "N3 中級", "title": "スーダン国境で金を探していた人々72人が空爆で死亡、人権団体が発表", "title_zh": "苏丹边境淘金者遭空袭，72人死亡，人权组织发声", "has_translation": true, "topic": "world", "source": "bbc_world", "source_url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cqy43vrk8wv8o?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1621837593522-eae4fc6a9f17?ixid=M3wxMDk3Mzk1fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8N3x8ZG96ZW5zJTIwZ29sZCUyMHByb3NwZWN0b3JzfGVufDB8MHx8fDE3OTE3NjYxMzJ8MA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&w=1600&q=75&fm=jpg&fit=max", "provider": "unsplash", "credit": "Photo by Kanchanara on Unsplash", "author": "Kanchanara", "credit_url": "https://unsplash.com/@kanchanara?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "source": "Unsplash", "source_url": "https://unsplash.com/photos/silver-and-black-round-pendant-necklace-tayj2w_LCHI?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "fallback": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(69, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(107, 46%, 48%)", "label": "WORLD", "seed": "8fb5b734dbc5"}}, "published_date": "2026-10-12", "word_count": 204, "reading_minutes": 0.6, "lead": "スーダンの首都ハルツームにある人権団体「緊急弁護士」は、スーダンとエジプトの国境近くで金を探していた少なくとも72人が空爆で死亡したと発表しました。エジプト政府とスーダンの実権当局はまだコメントしていません。", "lead_zh": "位于苏丹首都喀土穆的人权组织“紧急律师”表示，在苏丹与埃及边境附近淘金的至少72人死于空袭。埃及政府和苏丹实际掌权当局尚未对此发表评论。", "preview": "人権団体「緊急弁護士」によると、空爆は土曜日、スーダン北部のナイル川州にある金の採掘場で起きました。戦闘機が、手作りの道具で金を探す人たちを狙ったということです。エジプト政府もスーダンの実権当局も、今のところ何も言っていません。", "preview_zh": "据人权组织“紧急律师”称，空袭于周六发生在苏丹北部尼罗河州的一个金矿开采点。战机瞄准了用简易工具淘金的人们。埃及政府和苏丹实际掌权当局目前都没有发表任何评论。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 626, "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/64/ja_n3.mp3", "duration": 42.775, "size_bytes": 260352, "engine": "edge-tts", "voice": "ja-JP-NanamiNeural", "word_count": 138, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@d131376/content/data/versions/638.json", "paragraphs": ["人権団体「緊急弁護士」によると、空爆は土曜日、スーダン北部のナイル川州にある金の採掘場で起きました。戦闘機が、手作りの道具で金を探す人たちを狙ったということです。エジプト政府もスーダンの実権当局も、今のところ何も言っていません。", "この団体は日曜日の声明で、「武器を持たない民間人をわざと狙うのは国際人道法と生命の権利に反する。戦争犯罪になる可能性がある」と非難しました。また、死者の数はまだ途中の集計で、これから増えるかもしれないとしています。"], "paragraphs_zh": ["据人权组织“紧急律师”称，空袭于周六发生在苏丹北部尼罗河州的一个金矿开采点。战机瞄准了用简易工具淘金的人们。埃及政府和苏丹实际掌权当局目前都没有发表任何评论。", "该组织在周日的声明中谴责说：“故意针对手无寸铁的平民，违反国际人道法和生命权，可能构成战争罪。”此外，死亡人数只是初步统计，今后可能还会增加。"], "body": "人権団体「緊急弁護士」によると、空爆は土曜日、スーダン北部のナイル川州にある金の採掘場で起きました。戦闘機が、手作りの道具で金を探す人たちを狙ったということです。エジプト政府もスーダンの実権当局も、今のところ何も言っていません。\n\nこの団体は日曜日の声明で、「武器を持たない民間人をわざと狙うのは国際人道法と生命の権利に反する。戦争犯罪になる可能性がある」と非難しました。また、死者の数はまだ途中の集計で、これから増えるかもしれないとしています。", "body_zh": "据人权组织“紧急律师”称，空袭于周六发生在苏丹北部尼罗河州的一个金矿开采点。战机瞄准了用简易工具淘金的人们。埃及政府和苏丹实际掌权当局目前都没有发表任何评论。\n\n该组织在周日的声明中谴责说：“故意针对手无寸铁的平民，违反国际人道法和生命权，可能构成战争罪。”此外，死亡人数只是初步统计，今后可能还会增加。", "text": "人権団体「緊急弁護士」によると、空爆は土曜日、スーダン北部のナイル川州にある金の採掘場で起きました。戦闘機が、手作りの道具で金を探す人たちを狙ったということです。エジプト政府もスーダンの実権当局も、今のところ何も言っていません。 この団体は日曜日の声明で、「武器を持たない民間人をわざと狙うのは国際人道法と生命の権利に反する。戦争犯罪になる可能性がある」と非難しました。また、死者の数はまだ途中の集計で、これから増えるかもしれないとしています。", "vocab": [{"word": "空爆", "pos": "noun", "zh": "空袭", "note": "从飞机上进行的轰炸", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "国境", "pos": "noun", "zh": "边境、国界", "note": "国家与国家之间的边界", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "人権団体", "pos": "noun", "zh": "人权组织", "note": "从事人权活动的团体", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "採掘", "pos": "noun", "zh": "开采、挖掘", "note": "从地下挖出矿物等", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "民間人", "pos": "noun", "zh": "平民", "note": "不是军人的一般人", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "声明", "pos": "noun", "zh": "声明", "note": "公开表达意见的文章或发言", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "違反", "pos": "noun", "zh": "违反", "note": "不遵守法律或规则", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "戦争犯罪", "pos": "noun", "zh": "战争罪", "note": "战争中严重违反国际法的行为", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "集計", "pos": "noun", "zh": "统计、汇总", "note": "把数字汇总起来", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "目撃者", "pos": "noun", "zh": "目击者", "note": "亲眼看到事件的人", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "緊張", "pos": "noun", "zh": "紧张", "note": "关系或局势变得不安稳", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "密輸", "pos": "noun", "zh": "走私", "note": "违法秘密运输货物", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}], "title_original": "Dozens of gold prospectors killed in strikes on Egypt-Sudan border, rights group says", "summary_original": "Neither Egypt nor Sudan has commented on the alleged strikes on an artisanal mining camp on Saturday.", "body_original": "Dozens of gold prospectors killed in strikes on Egypt-Sudan border, rights group says\nBy\nAleks Phillips\nPublished\n3 hours ago\nAt least 72 civilians who had been prospecting for gold in a border region of Sudan have been killed in air strikes, a regional rights group says.\nEmergency Lawyers, based in the Sudanese capital, Khartoum, said jets targeted the so-called artisanal miners at a popular gold mining sites in Sudan's River Nile state on Saturday.\nNeither the Egyptian government nor the de facto Sudanese authorities have so far commented.\nCairo has previously faced accusations of deadly strikes on gold prospectors as part of a crackdown on illicit activity along its southern border.\nEmergency Lawyers noted the previous alleged attacks and said they represented not only a violation of Sudan's sovereign territory but demonstrated the government's lack of control over the region.\n\"The deliberate targeting of unarmed civilians violates international humanitarian law and the right to life,\" it said in a statement on Sunday. \"These acts may constitute war crimes.\"\nIt noted that its death toll was provisional and could rise.\nThe Paris-based Sudan Tribune reported that the death toll could far exceed the number reported by Emergency Lawyers, citing a survivor of Saturday's attack who said many more people had been injured.\nEyewitnesses said the attack began around 06:00 local time (04:00 GMT), with the aircraft firing more than five missiles directly at the miners' camps, destroying them and excavation pits with people still inside, the newspaper wrote.\nThe Sudan Tribune reported claims in June that Egyptian forces had used drones and artillery to target artisanal mining sites in the same region, killing several, after sporadic incidents of Egyptian border guards of burning equipment, torching temporary shelters, and firing live ammunition to disperse mine workers.\nDays later, Egypt's border agency announced that it and the military had begun a sweeping security campaign along the border to foil illegal migration, drug smuggling and illegal mining.\nAt the same time, Sudan's de facto leader announced an investigation into the alleged strikes, which were said to have killed dozens.\nGold lies at the core of the border tensions.\nSudan's ongoing civil war has led to a surge in artisanal mining - an often risky practice conducted by civilians with rudimentary tools and without official permission - particularly in remote areas near its borders.\nGold-rich areas such as those in River Nile state lie along porous borders in terrain historically associated with cross-border smuggling routes, with artisanally mined gold potentially feeding into those channels.\nEgypt's border force said in June that it had seized 86 tonnes of gold ore along with amateur prospecting equipment.\nArtisanal mining has also reportedly continued in Sudan's conflict zones and smuggled gold may be a source of income for armed insurgent groups.\nThis has raised concerns of illicit Sudanese gold undermining the legitimate Egyptian gold market.\nRelated topics\nSudan\nEgypt\nAfrica\nMining\nMore on this story\nA simple guide to what is happening in Sudan\nPublished\n13 November 2025", "fetched_at": "2026-10-12T00:48:50.607058", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "人権", "s": 0.125, "e": 0.637, "sm": 125, "em": 637, "cs": 0, "ce": 2, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "団体", "s": 0.65, "e": 1.163, "sm": 650, "em": 1162, "cs": 2, "ce": 4, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": "「", "s": 1.163, "e": 1.475, "sm": 1162, "em": 1475, "cs": 4, "ce": 5, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, "w"